# 6.18 mainline kernel for the Google Pixel 2 / 2 XL (MSM8998), built from
# pristine kernel.org v6.18 plus a numbered series, per the pmaports convention
# that a device kernel pins a release artifact rather than the tip of a fork.
#
# The series is the kernel this port is actually measured on: 11 generic
# msm8998 fixes that were only in the msm8998-mainline fork, the 32 device
# bring-up patches, and the 72 fixes that follow them (camera write path,
# audio/SLIMbus/APR, IPA, CPRh/OSM cpufreq, display, sensors, radios).
#
# 0093/0094 restore the osm_setup_stop/cprh_init_stop module params that a
# prior rebase dropped as "[BRINGUP] instrumentation": their default is 0,
# which is a safety gate, not a debug knob left on by accident. Programming
# the OSM/CPRh sequence unconditionally hangs MSM8998 with no console
# output (see qcom-cpufreq-hw.c:1531, cpr3.c:2551 and
# docs/campaign/KERNEL-BASE-RECONCILIATION.md D.0-D.6 upstream). Do not
# drop these two again without first proving the sequence is safe.
# 0175 is BRINGUP scaffolding and must be dropped before this series is
# published, together with CONFIG_SND_SOC_QDSP6_VOICE_DBG. It is a debugfs pipe
# to the ADSP voice services, and it exists only until a real q6voice driver is
# written -- see docs/CALL-AUDIO-2026-08-25.md for the specification it
# measured. 0173/0174 are ordinary DT patches and stay.
#
# Kernel config based on: taimen_defconfig
maintainer="Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>"
